? scenario: A screen can be Loading, Loaded with data, or Failed with an error. Which modelling gives compile-time safety when adding states later?
+ A sealed class with one subclass per state and an exhaustive switch
- A String field like 'loading'
- Three nullable fields and many if checks
- An int status code
> Sealed hierarchies make every state explicit and checked.
? mcq: What is the main difference between an enum and a sealed class?
+ Sealed subtypes can carry different fields; enum values share the same fields
- Enums can't be used in switches
