= false
> Throw typed exceptions so callers can catch them selectively.
? mcq: Which exception fits "the object is in the wrong state for this operation"?
- FormatException
+ StateError
- RangeError
- TimeoutException
> StateError signals an invalid state.
? fill: Custom recoverable exceptions should `implements ___`.
= Exception
> Implementing Exception marks the type as an expected, recoverable condition.
? scenario: Your try/catch around `fetchProfile();` (without await) never catches the failure. Why?
+ Without await, the error is delivered to the Future after the try block has already finished
- try/catch doesn't work in Dart
- The exception type is wrong
- finally swallowed it
> await is required for the try block to observe the Future's error.
